{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Except for his close relative.</b> It was stated in Torat Kohanim: 'the close one' and not the betrothed. And regarding his sister, Rashi explained: 'his close relative to him' — to include the betrothed, and this is what is difficult for him: since a priest does not defile himself for his betrothed, by the same reasoning he should defile himself for his betrothed sister, since if her husband were a priest he would not involve himself in her burial." "<b>To his brother and to his sister.</b> It was stated in Torat Kohanim: I might think to his brother and to his sister from the mother — Scripture says, ״לבנו ולבתו״; just as his son and daughter, who inherit, so too his brother and sister who inherit him — to exclude from the mother, who do not inherit."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:33.761569936Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}